  "key_concepts": [
    "Extrude SOP extends faces along normals and can create front, back, and side geometry with independent output types.",
    "The default extrusion direction is one unit backward from input normals, so source normals strongly affect results.",
    "A second input can provide a cross-section curve; only its X/Y coordinates are used and they are relative to the first vertex.",
